">for flavoring the pot</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">cup</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">vegetable broth</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">substitute for dry white wine</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">8</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">oz</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Gruyère cheese</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">grated</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">8</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">oz</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Emmental cheese</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">grated</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tablespoon</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">cornstarch</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">to thicken</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tablespoon</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">cherry juice</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">substitute for kirsch</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">to taste</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">freshly ground black pepper</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">to taste</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">freshly grated nutmeg</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">for a hint of spice</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">as needed</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">crusty bread cubes</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">for dipping</span></li></ul></div></div></div>\n      <div id=\"recipe-6990-equipment\" class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"6990\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-equipment-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Equipment</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-internal-container wprm-internal-container-equipment wprm-expandable-container wprm-expandable-expanded\" style=\"\"><div class=\"wprm-internal-container-toggle\"><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-show\" aria-label=\"Show Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,9.5 8,5 12.5,9.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"true\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-hide\" aria-label=\"Hide Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,6.5 8,11 12.5,6.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment wprm-recipe-equipment-list\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 Fondue pot&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For melting the cheese</span></div></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 Stove&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">To heat the fondue pot</span></div></li></ul></div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"wprm-layout-column wprm-column-width-50 meadow-main-right\">\n      <div id=\"recipe-6990-instructions\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions-container wprm-recipe-6990-instructions-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"6990\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-instructions-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-spacer wprm-header-has-actions\" style=\"\">Method<div class=\"wprm-decoration-spacer\"></div>&nbsp;</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Instructions</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ol class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions\"><li id=\"wprm-recipe-6990-step-0-0\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 1: Rub the pot &#8211; Take a clove of garlic and rub the inside of your fondue pot. Discard the garlic once done. This will infuse a lovely flavor into your cheese fondue.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-6990-step-0-1\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 2: Heat the base &#8211; Place the pot on the stove and pour in some non-alcoholic white wine or vegetable broth. Heat it over medium heat until it starts to simmer gently.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-6990-step-0-2\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 3: Add the cheese &#8211; In a bowl, toss your favorite cheeses with cornstarch. Gradually add this cheesy mixture to the simmering liquid, stirring constantly until it melts and becomes smooth.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-6990-step-0-3\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 4: Season it up &#8211; Stir in a splash of non-alcoholic cherry juice, a pinch of pepper, and a dash of nutmeg. This will elevate the flavors and make your fondue irresistible!</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-6990-step-0-4\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 5: Serve and enjoy &#8211; Keep the fondue warm over low heat. Serve it with cubes of bread for dipping. Enjoy the gooey goodness with friends!</span></div></li></ol></div></div>\n      \n      \n      <div id=\"recipe-6990-notes\" class=\"wprm-recipe-notes-container wprm-block-text-normal\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-notes-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Notes</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-notes\"><table>\n<tr>\n<th>Nutrient</th>\n<th>Amount per Serving</th>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Calories</td>\n<td>350</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Fat</td>\n<td>25g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Protein</td>\n<td>20g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Carbs</td>\n<td>15g</td>\n</tr>\n</table></div></div>\n      <div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 40px;\"></div>\n      \n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div></div></div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"ingredients\"><strong>Ingredients</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Gather these delicious ingredients for a delightful cheese <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fondue\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">fondue </a>experience!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Cheese-Fondue-Ingredients-Display.webp\" alt=\"A rustic cheese fondue setup with melted cheese, garlic, cherry juice, and bread cubes for dipping.\" class=\"wp-image-6988\" srcset=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Cheese-Fondue-Ingredients-Display.webp 400w, /wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Cheese-Fondue-Ingredients-Display-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>1 clove garlic</strong> – for flavoring the pot</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 cup vegetable broth</strong> – substitute for dry white wine</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>8 oz Gruyère cheese</strong> – grated</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>8 oz Emmental cheese</strong> – grated</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 tablespoon cornstarch</strong> – to thicken</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 tablespoon cherry juice</strong> – substitute for kirsch</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>freshly ground black pepper</strong> – to taste</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>freshly grated nutmeg</strong> – for a hint of spice</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>crusty bread cubes</strong> – for dipping</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-make-cheese-fondue\"><strong>How to Make cheese fondue</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Get ready for a delightful cheese fondue experience! This recipe takes about 10 minutes to prepare and 15 minutes to cook, making it a quick and fun dish to enjoy with friends. Gather your favorite dippables and let’s get started!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Step-by-Step-Cheese-Fondue-Preparation.webp\" alt=\"Step-by-step process of making cheese fondue, showcasing garlic, simmering wine, cheese mixture, and bread cubes.\" class=\"wp-image-6989\" srcset=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Step-by-Step-Cheese-Fondue-Preparation.webp 400w, /wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Step-by-Step-Cheese-Fondue-Preparation-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 1: Rub the pot</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Take a clove of garlic and rub the inside of your fondue pot. Discard the garlic once done. This will infuse a lovely flavor into your cheese fondue.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 2: Heat the base</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Place the pot on the stove and pour in some non-alcoholic white wine or vegetable broth. Heat it over medium heat until it starts to simmer gently.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 3: Add the cheese</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">In a bowl, toss your favorite cheeses with cornstarch. Gradually add this cheesy mixture to the simmering liquid, stirring constantly until it melts and becomes smooth.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 4: Season it up</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Stir in a splash of non-alcoholic cherry juice, a pinch of pepper, and a dash of nutmeg. This will elevate the flavors and make your fondue irresistible!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 5: Serve and enjoy</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Keep the fondue warm over low heat. Serve it with cubes of bread for dipping. Enjoy the gooey goodness with friends!</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"recipe-snapshot\"><strong>Recipe Snapshot</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Details</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Category</td><td>Appetizer / dinner</td></tr><tr><td>Cuisine</td><td>Swiss</td></tr><tr><td>Prep Time</td><td>10 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Cook Time</td><td>15 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Extra Time</td><td>0 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Total Time</td><td>25 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Dietary</td><td>Vegetarian</td></tr><tr><td>Serves</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>Best Served</td><td>Warm with crusty bread cubes</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"pro-tips-for-making-cheese-fondue\"><strong>Pro Tips for Making cheese fondue</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Grate your cheese for a smoother melt.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Use low-sodium vegetable broth instead of wine.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Stir continuously to prevent clumping.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Keep the heat low to avoid burning.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Serve with a variety of dippables for fun flavors.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-serve-this-cheese-fondue\"><strong>How to Serve this cheese fondue</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Pair with fresh, crusty bread for a classic dip.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Serve alongside an array of colorful veggies like bell peppers, broccoli, and cherry tomatoes.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Include bite-sized pieces of cooked potatoes for a hearty option.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Try dipping apple slices or pear wedges for a sweet twist.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Offer pretzel bites for a fun, salty crunch.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Use tortilla chips for a unique, crunchy alternative.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Set out a variety of dippable meats like grilled chicken or turkey slices.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>For a twist, serve with popcorn for a cheesy snack experience.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"make-ahead-and-storage\"><strong>Make Ahead and Storage</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Storing and enjoying your cheese fondue later is easy!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Storing cheese fondue Leftovers</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Allow fondue to cool to room temperature.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Transfer to an airtight container.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Store in the refrigerator for up to 3 days.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Freezing cheese fondue</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Cool fondue completely before freezing.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Use a freezer-safe container or bag.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Label with date; freeze for up to 2 months.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Reheating cheese fondue</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Thaw in the refrigerator overnight if frozen.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Reheat gently on the stove over low heat.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Add a splash of vegetable broth for creaminess.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Stir frequently to maintain smooth texture.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Explore more easy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/breakfast/\"><strong>breakfast</strong></a> recipes, quick <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/lunch/\"><strong>lunch</strong></a> ideas, cozy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dinner/\"><strong>dinner</strong></a> meals, tasty <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/snacks/\"><strong>snacks</strong></a>, and delightful <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dessert/\"><strong>dessert</strong></a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"fa-qs\"><strong>FAQs</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here’s a helpful FAQ about this recipe:</p>\n\n\n<div id=\"rank-math-faq\" class=\"rank-math-block\">\n<div class=\"rank-math-list \">\n<div id=\"faq-question-1\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>1. What do you put in a cheese fondue?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>A classic cheese fondue typically includes a blend of cheeses, such as Gruyère and Emmental, melted together with a bit of cornstarch for thickness. You can also add garlic for flavor and a splash of vegetable broth or non-alcoholic white wine as a substitute for traditional wine. This combination creates a creamy, delicious dip that’s perfect for sharing!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-2\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>2. What are the 4 cheeses in fondue?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>While there are many variations, a popular combination for cheese fondue includes Gruyère, Emmental, Fontina, and a touch of cream cheese for extra creaminess. Each cheese brings its unique flavor and texture, creating a rich and delightful experience that pairs beautifully with dippers!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-3\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>3. What do you eat with cheese fondue?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Cheese fondue is incredibly versatile! You can enjoy it with a variety of dippers such as crusty bread, fresh vegetables like broccoli and carrots, or even cooked potatoes. For a fun twist, try dipping apple slices or pretzels for a sweet and salty combination that complements the cheese perfectly!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-4\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>4. What is the secret to good fondue?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>The secret to a great cheese fondue lies in the quality of your cheese and the right melting technique. Always use freshly grated cheese for the best texture and flavor. Additionally, heating the cheese slowly and stirring continuously helps achieve that smooth, velvety consistency that makes fondue so irresistible!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"final-thoughts\"><strong>Final Thoughts</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Cheese fondue is not just a dish; it&#8217;s an experience! Gather your loved ones, dip your favorite bread, and savor the gooey goodness. It&#8217;s simple, fun, and oh-so-rewarding. So, grab your cheese and let the melting magic begin! You’ll create delicious memories that will warm your heart and fill your belly. Enjoy every cheesy bite!</p>\n",
